1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[Kurapika] To verify, are you Pakunoda
of the Phantom Troupe?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Yes, I am.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
She's telling the truth.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Let's begin.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
I will present each of you
with two conditions.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
If you choose to abide by them,
I will release your leader.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
[Chrollo] Figure it out, Pakunoda.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
He's more concerned about his friends
than killing me to satisfy his revenge.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
That is the chain user's weakness!

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
[theme music playing]

11
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,000
SIGNAL x TO x RETREAT

12
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[Kurapika] I’ll start with the conditions
for the leader.

13
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
First, I hereby forbid
all further use of Nen.

14
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
[breathing shakily]

15
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Is this really the right move?

16
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
If I eliminate the boss,
the Spider will fall apart.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
That was the idea, but...

18
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
I have absolutely no value as a hostage.

19
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Everything that he’s saying
right now is true.

20
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
[Kurapika] But the Spider can live on,
even without a head.

21
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
The leader isn't everything.

22
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The group would be more than willing

23
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
to sacrifice him
if they felt it necessary.

24
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
That is the nature of the Phantom Troupe.

25
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
I can cut off the head,
but it’s no guarantee the spider will die.

26
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
The question is,
is there any other alternative?

27
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Is there some kind of miracle
that can get me out of this bind?

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
[sighs] There isn't.
None that I can think of.

29
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Yes, this is right.

30
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
In this moment, this is what I have to do.

31
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,000
I must get those two back.
That is my top priority!

32
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
I’ve lost too many people already.

33
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,000
I will not lose my friends!

34
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Second, I forbid all contact
with other Troupe members from now on.

35
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Those are my conditions.

36
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
And to make certain you adhere to them,

37
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
I will stab your leader
with my Judgment Chain:

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Arbiter Little Finger.

39
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
It’s up to you now, Pakunoda.
Are these conditions acceptable?

40
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Yes, I accept.

41
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
[Kurapika] Pakunoda, you're next.

42
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:19,000
First off, release Gon and Killua,
uninjured, before midnight,

43
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
and without any deceptions.

44
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Second, you are also forbidden
to reveal anything about me.

45
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Accept and I’ll stab you
with the chain as well.

46
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Yes, go ahead.

47
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
-[chain rattling]
-[grunts]

48
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Hey, if Gon and Killua
were being controlled by a Manipulator,

49
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
could you tell from their heartbeats?

50
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
[Melody] Maybe.

51
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
I've met Killua before,
so I know his normal heartbeat.

52
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
I should be able to tell
if anything has changed.

53
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Good enough.

54
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Before the exchange,
I have something to say.

55
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
[heart beating]

56
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
[Melody] Kurapika.

57
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
In the back of your mind,
you sense that something's amiss.

58
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
You’re curious as to why Pakunoda
came alone.

59
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,000
If the Troupe were as merciless
as we expected them to be,

60
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
this hostage exchange would be impossible.

61
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[Chrollo] You are the one who is cornered.

62
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[Melody] Their rules are ironclad

63
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
and their boss accepts them
without question.

64
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
But what about the others?

65
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
This one appears to be different.

66
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
This woman whom you despise

67
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
with your whole being
is driven, certainly.

68
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:43,000
But by the very same motive
that drives you.

69
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,000
She wishes to save her boss...
to save her friend.

70
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
You do realize this, don’t you?

71
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Now, return to your companions
and inform them of the exchange.

72
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
I want you to bring the hostages
to Lingon Airport before midnight tonight.

73
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Come alone and tell no one
where you're going.

74
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
I understand. I will do what you ask.

75
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Take me back to the airport.

76
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
You haven't asked any questions.

77
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:26,000
You know who I am. You must by now.
Aren't you worried?

78
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
You don't find this deal unreasonable?

79
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Do you actually believe
I'll return your leader?

80
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
-I do.
-[Kurapika gasps]

81
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
If you really wanted to deceive me,

82
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
you wouldn’t have asked me
those questions.

83
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
[thunder crashing]

84
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Does he really expect us
to simply accept those conditions?

85
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Tell us where he is, Paku.

86
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:59,000
We'll kill the kids and go deal
with the chain user.

87
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
You’re insisting?

88
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Damn right I am.

89
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
If you don’t tell us,
then you’re not leaving.

90
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
I refuse to tell you anything,

91
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
and I’m taking the kids alone,
end of story.

92
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Don't interfere.

93
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Screw that. If anyone is interfering,
it’s you!

94
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Go ahead, Pakunoda.
We can stop them, so don't worry.

95
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Stop us? How insulting.

96
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,000
[Phinks] You’re serious, aren’t you?
I don’t get it.

97
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Have you all lost your damn minds?

98
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[Feitan] I think the chain user got
to them before we arrived.

99
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
They're probably under his control.

100
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
We're wasting time.
I'll make them talk.

101
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
[Gon] You really don't get it?

102
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
You don't understand why Pakunoda
wants to leave

103
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
without telling you anything?

104
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
And you don’t understand
why Machi would wanna stop you?

105
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
You think it’s because
they’re being manipulated?

106
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
It’s ‘cause they wanna rescue your boss!
What else would it be?

107
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
They wanna save their friend from danger.
Don’t you understand that?

108
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Shut up, pipsqueak!
You're just desperate to leave!

109
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Gon grunting]

110
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I’m not saying it to save myself.
Take it back!

111
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
[Killua] Man...

112
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
[chains breaking]

113
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Take it back?
Come over here and make me.

114
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
I’ll rip your head off
the second you take a step.

115
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Then I won’t! You think I’m that stupid?

116
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Kurapika isn't like you.

117
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
No matter how much he hates someone,

118
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
he would never lose control
and kill them out of anger!

119
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
He’s not a murderer!

120
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
And you better believe
if Kurapika makes a promise,

121
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,000
then he’s gonna keep his word,
no matter what happens.

122
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Doubt me? Ask Pakunoda.
She’s met him. She knows!

123
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
If you just do what he says,
he will return your boss!

124
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
[Phinks] All right kid, that's enough.

125
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
I’m starting to get real sick
of your crap!

126
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[Franklin] Knock it off!

127
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Just let Pakunoda go.

128
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[Phinks]
What, you're siding with them now?

129
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Hey, Shal, what do you think
our worst-case scenario would be?

130
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Hmm, that the Boss is already dead

131
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
and Paku and the rest
are being controlled.

132
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
That we won’t be able
to locate the chain user

133
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
and the two kids find a way to escape.

134
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
[Franklin] You've got it all wrong.

135
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:22,000
The worst-case scenario is that we all die
and the Spider perishes.

136
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:26,000
What you’re talking about
would be pretty pleasant by comparison.

137
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Am I wrong?

138
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
No, you're right.

139
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Whatever your reasoning,
you’re relying way too much on the boss.

140
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
And if the Phantom Troupe falls apart
as a result,

141
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
that’d be more of a betrayal
than anything else.

142
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Keep bickering like this
and it might just happen.

143
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
So calm down and let them have their way.

144
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Pakunoda can take the kids.

145
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
If the boss doesn't return,

146
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
we’ll kill the members
who are being controlled

147
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:59,000
and start rebuilding the spider.
It's really that simple.

148
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
[Machi]
I'm fine with that if it'll satisfy you.

149
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Though I’m not being controlled
and killing me won’t be easy.

150
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[scoffs]

151
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
[phone ringing]

152
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
-Yeah, hello--
-[Kurapika] Put the hostages on the phone.

153
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
[Shalnark] Don't break it!

154
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[Kurapika] Are you okay?
Are they there?

155
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Yeah, they're all right here.

156
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[Shalnark] Hey!

157
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Look, we're following your orders.

158
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[Franklin] Aren't you going
to go after them?

159
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
I mean, the chain user can’t monitor
our location now.

160
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[Phinks] Shut up.

161
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
If I tried to follow them,
you would just stop me, right?

162
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
I’ll just wait here for the time being.

163
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
And if the Boss doesn’t come back
for whatever reason,

164
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
I guess I’ll kill you, too.

165
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
[Franklin] As you wish.

166
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
[Kurapika] Board the airship.
The pilot knows where to go.

167
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
[Melody]
Just the three of them, as promised.

168
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
[Kurapika] We can't be sure yet.

169
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
So stay on high alert.

170
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
There's someone over there.

171
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
[phone ringing]

172
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
It's him! Hisoka!

173
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,000
[Hisoka] Hey.

174
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
What are you doing here?
Did you sneak out?

175
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:20,000
No need for concern.
I left a double behind.

176
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[Illumi] Make it quick. Without needles,
my face will revert in four to five hours.

177
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
[Kurapika] What are you up to?

178
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[Hisoka] Allow me to board the airship
with them.

179
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
If you refuse, I'll kill Gon and Killua.

180
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[Kurapika] Bastard.

181
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,000
[Hisoka] I’m only kidding.
I would never be so wasteful.

182
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
My target is Chrollo and Chrollo alone.

183
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:47,000
And I’ll gladly get off the airship
as soon as he is released.

184
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
All I want is to fight him.
Nothing more, I promise.

185
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
[phone ringing]

186
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
[Kurapika] Killua, place the phone
next to your heart.

187
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
It’s fine. There’s nothing wrong with him.

188
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Okay. Begin the exchange!

189
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,000
[Kurapika] If you make contact
with a Troupe member, you die.

190
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Now you'll know the pain...

191
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
of losing your home.

192
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
[Hisoka] I've waited a long time
for this moment.

193
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Come on. Let's fight.

194
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
I won’t be needing this anymore.

195
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Now this won’t be considered infighting.
So there’s no need to hold back.

196
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:29,000
[chuckles] We can talk
because you aren't a Troupe member.

197
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
I can't fight you.

198
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Or rather, I’m simply not worth
the trouble.

199
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Because, you see,

200
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,000
he stabbed his Judgment Chain
directly into my heart.

201
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
I can't use Nen anymore.

202
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
[wind whistling]

203
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
It appears that we can leave now.

204
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
I see.

205
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Leorio] Hisoka returned to the airship
without fighting at all.

206
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[Kurapika] The leader probably told him
about my chains

207
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
once he realized he wasn’t a member.

208
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
But I’m not surprised.

209
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Fighting someone who can’t use Nen
wouldn’t be of much interest to Hisoka.

210
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
So wait, he wasn't a Troupe member?

211
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
No.

212
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[Pakunoda] How did you sneak out?

213
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
[Hisoka]
I have a friend who's good with disguises.

214
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
There’s no need to worry.

215
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
I no longer have any reason
to kill Chrollo.

216
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
I have no interest in broken toys.

217
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
“Slip out when it pleases you.”

218
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
One more thing.

219
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,000
My real fortune mentioned something.

220
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
That I would have a date
with the boss on Tuesday.

221
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:43,000
It also said that by the time I left,
the Troupe’s numbers would be cut in half.

222
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Bit by bit, fate seems to be changing.

223
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[Kurapika]
I’m sorry for exposing you to danger.

224
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
You used your chains on the boss,
didn’t you?

225
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
[Kurapika] Yes, but...

226
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Something tells me
that this isn’t the end.

227
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[cat meows]

228
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Meow.

229
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[Phinks] Where's the boss?

230
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[Pakunoda] He can’t come here.

231
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Huh? You’re kidding. You’d better explain.

232
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
And if we don’t like it…
[cracking knuckles]

233
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Yes, I know. But don’t worry.

234
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:37,000
I can only shoot six bullets at once.
Enough for the founding members.

235
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Feitan, Phinks, Machi, Nobunaga,
Shalnark, Franklin...

236
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Will you trust me,
and accept this completely?

237
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
[Machi] Paku, you're not...

238
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Hey! Don’t tell me
you’re being controlled--

239
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Be quiet!

240
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
It's Paku. You can trust her.

241
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
[Pakunoda] All my memories...

242
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
My heart and soul...

243
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
I give you everything.

244
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,000
[bullets firing]

245
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[gasping]

246
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Please...

247
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Let me be...

248
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
the last.

249
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Paku... [grunts]

250
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
[Shizuku] She's dead.

251
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
What's going on here?

252
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
[Phinks] I’ll explain everything.

253
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
[thunder rumbling]

254
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Now we know. She did this because…

255
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[Gon] I sure hope Kurapika's fever
doesn't go down.

256
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
[Killua] Yeah.

257
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Hold on. What did you just say?

258
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:16,000
[Gon] I feel like Kurapika shouldn’t fight
the Phantom Troupe anymore.

259
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,000
[Killua] Huh?

260
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,000
[Gon] When he told me about his abilities,
I thought of something.

261
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,000
If all he had really wanted
was to get revenge,

262
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,000
then he probably would have
taken on different abilities.

263
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
[Killua] Think so?

264
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I do. Because If he had only wanted
to kill the Troupe,

265
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:36,000
he wouldn’t have gone through the trouble
of chaining their hearts. I wouldn't have.

266
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Maybe, if he only had one target.

267
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Instead, he was dealing with all of them.
He couldn’t catch and kill one right away.

268
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
He’d need to extract information
about the others.

269
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[Gon] Oh.

270
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:54,000
[Killua] I think his ability was created
solely for revenge.

271
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
I see.

272
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:01,000
But that was his original objective.
Kurapika's different now.

273
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,000
I'm blessed with good friends.

274
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
[Killua] But you've got a point.

275
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
He really should stay still
for a little while.

276
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
If their boss doesn’t come back,

277
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
they’re gonna be even more determined
to find him.

278
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,000
[Gon] Yeah.

279
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
[Killua] Either way,
we’re gonna have to be careful

280
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,000
when we go to the auction house.

281
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
-So, do you really have a plan?
-[gasps]

282
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Something to help us get our hands
on Greed Island?

283
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,000
'Cause that’s all we have to go on!

284
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Uh, yeah, but it's only a 50-50 chance.

285
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Wait, didn’t you say 70 percent earlier?

286
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
I get it. That's pretty clever.

287
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
And it might be our only shot.

288
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
It’s practical and sound, too.

289
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Yeah! The way I see it,
our odds are 80 percent!

290
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,000
-Really?
-Really. Let's do it.

291
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[Gon] The auction is in Hall B.

292
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,000
[Killua] That's it, over there.

293
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[Gon] Wow!

294
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[both startle]

295
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[both grunting]

296
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
What the heck are those guys doing here?

297
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
How would I know?

298
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
[Phinks] You know, that was cold.
No need for you to run away.

299
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
[Killua] Why wouldn't we run?

300
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Yeah, don't worry.

301
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,000
We’re not here to kill you two
or anything.

302
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:30,000
He’s right. It’s not like we can kill
the chain user now anyway.

303
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
[Gon] What? What do you mean?

304
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,000
[Phinks] Well, he used his chains
on the boss, didn’t he?

305
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
That means we can’t kill him.

306
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,000
I thought it was the opposite.

307
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
[Killua] It’s nice to have someone around

308
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
who never shies away
from asking questions.

309
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
When you die, it doesn’t mean
your Nen disappears.

310
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Nen that's driven by hatred and regret
can last a long time after death.

311
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
And it will direct itself
toward the target of those emotions.

312
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Since the boss can’t use Nen
himself anymore,

313
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
he’s all the more vulnerable
to that kind of assault.

314
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Scary, that residual Nen.

315
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,000
That's why we can't kill the chain user.

316
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Am I talking too much?

317
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Fine, then. I won't say another word.

318
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:25,000
There are Nen users a few, anyway,
who can remove Nen from other people.

319
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
[wind whistling]

320
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
[Chrollo] Hmm. East it is.

321
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
So, as you might’ve guessed,

322
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
we’re pretty much done
with the two of you.

323
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
The only reason we’re even here
is to enjoy the auction.

324
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
The other members decided
to pack up and go home already.

325
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Hold on. How's Miss Pakunoda?

326
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,000
She died, actually.

327
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Oh, I see.

328
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[Pakunoda] I don't get it.
Why don't you run away?

329
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
What do you mean by that?

330
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
[Pakunoda] With my injuries,
you could escape easily.

331
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,000
And if you did, I would lose my leverage,
and the chain user could kill the boss.

332
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
So why not run away?

333
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Aren't you on his side?

334
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Well, we’re his friends!

335
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,000
And we all care about him.

336
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:17,000
And we don’t want him to turn
into a murderer.

337
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:20,000
If an exchange will do the job,
that’s what we’ll do.

338
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
-[Gon] What's wrong?
-[Killua] Let's go.

339
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,000
[Phinks] Paku...

340
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Paku was very thankful to both of you.

341
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[narrator] Tune in next time,
when the Greed Island arc begins!

342
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:52,000
[theme music playing]

343
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,000
-[Gon] Coming up, Gon...
-[Killua] And Killua's...

344
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

345
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I'm Gon!
-I'm Killua!

346
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

347
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Today, we're introducing Chrollo!

348
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
He's a Specialist and the boss
of the Phantom Troupe!

349
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,000
He can steal other people's powers
for himself with his Skill Hunter!

350
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,000
As long as certain conditions are met.

351
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Huh. East it is.

352
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
[Gon] Next time: "Bid x and x Haste."

353
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] A bid in haste makes a whole lot
of waste. Hey!

354
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Killua] And a bad aftertaste.
